ll,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.09111830402869592,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":3.6,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.026389964933760043,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":40.4,"_gate_share_shrink":0.012470115157090955,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":34.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.45867002,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Merchants Bancorp operates as the diversified bank holding company in the United States. It operates through three segments: Multi-family Mortgage Banking, Mortgage Warehousing, and Banking. The Multi-family Mortgage Banking segment engages in the mortgage banking, which originates, and services government sponsored mortgages, including bridge financing products to refinance, acquire, or reposition multi-family housing projects, and construction lending for housing development and healthcare facilities financing. This segment also offers customized loan products for need-based skilled nursing facilities, such as independent living, assisted living, and memory care; and tax credit equity syndicator service. The Mortgage Warehousing segment funds agency eligible residential loans, as well as commercial loans to non-depository financial institutions. The Banking segment offers a range of financial products and services to consumers and businesses, which includes retail banking, commercial lending, agricultural lending, retail and correspondent residential mortgage banking, and small business administration lending. Merchants Bancorp was founded in 1990 and is headquartered in Carmel, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael J. Dunlap | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 735 people. Revenue per employee of $927K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 25%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Merchants Bancorp is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.3B market cap on $681M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $362M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.6% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 46% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Price sits 20% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2021771056325491},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 10% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"How (MBIN) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/How_MBIN_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_111226103601_1794497761.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497761.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Andrew Juster Awarded 342 Merchants Bancorp Shares in Quarterly Director Retainer","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/andrew-juster-awarded-342-merchants-bancorp-shares-in-quarterly-director-retainer","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795214999.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":1,